    dbp:artist <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pablo_Picasso> ;
    dbp:city <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Melbourne> ;
    dbp:heightMetric 55 ;
    dbp:imageFile "National Gallery of Victoria Weeping Woman.jpg"@en ;
    dbp:italicTitle "no"@en ;
    dbp:medium <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oil_painting> ;
    dbp:museum <http://dbpedia.org/resource/National_Gallery_of_Victoria> ;
    dbp:source "--08-05"^^xsd:gMonthDay ;
    dbp:text 1,
        2,
        "Australian Cultural Terrorists"@en,
        "Because the Minister of the Arts is also Minister of Plod, we are allowing him a sporting seven days in which to try to have us arrested while he deliberates.  There will be no negotiation. At the end of seven days if our demands have not been met the painting will be destroyed and our campaign continue."@en,
        "Two conditions must be publicly agreed upon if the painting is to be returned."@en,
        "We have stolen the Picasso from the National Gallery as a protest against the niggardly funding of the fine arts in this hick State and against the clumsy, unimaginitive stupidity of the administration and distribution of that funding."@en,
        "Your very humble servants,"@en ;
    dbp:title "\"The Ransom Letter\""@en,
        "The National Gallery of Victoria's Weeping Woman"@en ;
