    dbp:museum "Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, New York"@en ;
    dbp:owner "Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, New York"@en,
        "Thannhauser Collection, Gift, Justin Thannhauser, 1978"@en ;
    dbp:source "Souvenirs sans fin,1955.170"@en ;
    dbp:text "A petrol lamp was burning on a table carved in bourgeois taste with Second Empire moldings, which [Picasso] had bought at a junk shop. there was no question of electricity or even gas at 13 [Rue Ravignan]. The petrol lamp gave out little light. In order to paint and to display his canvases, a candle was necessary—that guttering candle which Picasso held up high in front of me when he gave me a human introduction to the superhuman world of these starving people, these and mothers with no milk, the superreal world of bleue Misère."@en ;
